{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover","id":1049468,"title":"Supernal Vision & Crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-15T14:04:07-08:00","id":1049468,"title":"Supernal Vision & Crossover","content":"There doesn't seem to be any specific clarification in the books, so I was hoping that the community would have some suggestions on how to handle this.<br /> Supernal Vision (Prime 1) can reveal which supernal realm a being is most connected to. While this is obviously meant to be a Mage's Path, could it also include general information about other supernaturals - do Vampires seem distantly related to Stygia, for example, or does it simply turn up with &quot;not applicable&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'm specifically curious about reading Sleepwalkers with this spell. It will inform if a person is a Sleeper or Sleepwalker, which implies that Sleepwalkers have a closer connection to the supernal. Would they ever have an affiliation with a particular Path (if they were going to Awaken, or revealing which Path their thoughts and actions primarily resonate with)?<br /> Or would you rule it instead as &quot;Sleepers are resonant with the Abyss; Sleepwalkers with nothing&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'm curious to hear peoples thoughts on this.<br /> Thanks,<br /> ~Seraph","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:10:14-08:00","id":1049472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover#post1049468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There doesn't seem to be any specific clarification in the books, so I was hoping that the community would have some suggestions on how to handle this.<br /> Supernal Vision (Prime 1) can reveal which supernal realm a being is most connected to. ~Seraph</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal Vision doesn't do that.<br /> <br /> In fact Supernal Vision doesn't reveal degrees of connection to the Supernal at all, just that there may be a connection or the existence of a supernatural phenomena within the Mage's view (Expanded to all supernatural phenomena with the +1 Reach).<br /> <br /> Which Supernal Realm a target is most closely connected to would be an ST call. Most people (Sleepwalkers included) would have a stronger resonance with one Supernal realm than another. Most supernatural creatures would apparently appear as a nonsensical jumble if the Mage is unfamiliar with the kind of aura they might exude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-15-2017, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:31:19-08:00","id":1049496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2e pg 166</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By studying a person, place, or location for one turn, the subject automatically knows whether it is connected to the Supernal (e.g. if a person is a mage, a Sleepwalker, a Proximus, or a Sleeper; if a place is a Demesne or Verge; if an object is Imbued, Enhanced, or an Artifact)</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpret that as the spell will distinguish between mages, sleepwalkers, proximus, and sleepers - revealing which one a subject is. Which implies a degree of connection.<br /> <br /> It sounds like you may be reading that as it doesn't distinguish between those categories, it will just say &quot;the person has/does not have a connection to the supernal&quot; and other means are needed to determine what they are on that spectrum ....? is that how you interpret the phrasing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:05:44-08:00","id":1049517,"title":"","content":"Yeah, pretty much, the list there is just examples of things that might be connected to the Supernal, not things that the spell reveals specifically. Note that the followup questions can give greater info, which may or may not clue you in to the subject's true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:32:07-08:00","id":1049563,"title":"","content":"Sleepwalkers, if they're the type with a Supernatural Merit or a minor-template like ghouls and Wolf-Blooded, would appear to resonate with whatever Realm that quality resonates with. Psychokinetics would be Aethereal, Wolf-Blooded would be Primal, the Atariya are Arcadian, and so on.<br /> <br /> A quick run down on what I think corresponds to the major templates:<ul><li>Vampires: Stygia and Pandemonium</li> <li>Werewolves: The Primal Wild</li> <li>Prometheans: Stygia and Aether</li> <li>Changelings: Arcadia and Pandemonium</li> <li>Sin-Eaters: Stygia</li> <li>Mummies: Depends on Decree; Bull-Aether, Falcon-Pandemonium, Jackal-Stygia, Lion-Primal, Serpent-Arcadia</li> <li>Demons: Aether and Arcadia</li> <li>Beasts: Pandemonium and the Primal Wild</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:41:54-08:00","id":1049569,"title":"","content":"I don't know. That wording makes either interpretation likely, and I think that's a very strict way of reading it - which would make identifying Sleepwalkers in particular quite difficult. Neither Mage Sight nor other spells would work to identify one. I can only imagine it coming down to Supernal Vision showing no connection, and then casting obvious magic to find out their reaction. That seems far too dangerous and difficult, especially in the context of their role in the Orders and that Second Edition emphasized their considerable numbers.<br /> Although I do suppose that the Sleepwalker Merit is by far the least populous source of Sleepwalkers - inborn talent being far more likely, and far easier to recognize..<br /> <br /> At the point of arguing nuance like this, though, it likely comes down to person preference anyway...<br /> <br /> At any rate, thank you for your perspective - it certainly gives me more to consider. You answered the heart of my question, by suggesting most people resonating with a particular Supernal realm more than others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:14:06-08:00","id":1049593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1049569#post1049569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. That wording makes either interpretation likely, and I think that's a very strict way of reading it - which would make identifying Sleepwalkers in particular quite difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if the first question you asked is, &quot;What is the target's Gnosis?&quot; The answer being 0 would immediately identify the person as a Sleepwalker at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:27:00-08:00","id":1049600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1049517#post1049517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, pretty much, the list there is just examples of things that might be connected to the Supernal, not things that the spell reveals specifically. Note that the followup questions can give greater info, which may or may not clue you in to the subject's true nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just out of curiosity - if that's a list of examples of things that might be connected to the Supernal, why would it list Sleepers in that list of examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T19:02:37-08:00","id":1049644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1049600#post1049600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity - if that's a list of examples of things that might be connected to the Supernal, why would it list Sleepers in that list of examples?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell actually says it identifies &quot;whether&quot; a subject is connected to the Supernal. In the case of a Sleeper you would get a negative response. Same would go for other supernatural creatures like werewolves and vampires, and if you tried to read deeper on those by using the Reach clause you get a jumble of confusing information that doesn't actually make any sense unless you've examined more of their kind to get some kind of context and even then it would just be, &quot;Oh, this thing looks like that other thing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-15-2017, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T03:02:35-08:00","id":1049771,"title":"","content":"I don't think the wording should be interpreted as 'automatically knows if they are a Mage/Sleepwalker/Proximus or if they are a Sleeper' because Proximus is a subset of Sleepwalkers. I think it makes more sense for the spell to distinguish between all four. Both Mages and Proximi have different kinds of connections to the Supernal. Sleepwalkers other than Proximi don't have any connection to the Supernal, but they also don't suffer Quiescence like Sleepers. It's definitely something a Prime Unveiling spell should be able to distinguish and there's no reason to be forced to cast a different Unveiling or Knowing spell with that kind of major overlap with this spell.<br /> In this case all major templates (aside from Mages, of course) would show up as Sleepwalkers even without the Reach option, but that should be the extent of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T03:07:34-08:00","id":1049773,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> that's what the follow-up questions are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:52:11-08:00","id":1050038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1049563#post1049563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleepwalkers, if they're the type with a Supernatural Merit or a minor-template like ghouls and Wolf-Blooded, would appear to resonate with whatever Realm that quality resonates with. Psychokinetics would be Aethereal, Wolf-Blooded would be Primal, the Atariya are Arcadian, and so on.<br /> <br /> A quick run down on what I think corresponds to the major templates:<ul><li>Vampires: Stygia and Pandemonium</li> <li>Werewolves: The Primal Wild</li> <li>Prometheans: Stygia and Aether</li> <li>Changelings: Arcadia and Pandemonium</li> <li>Sin-Eaters: Stygia</li> <li>Mummies: Depends on Decree; Bull-Aether, Falcon-Pandemonium, Jackal-Stygia, Lion-Primal, Serpent-Arcadia</li> <li>Demons: Aether and Arcadia</li> <li>Beasts: Pandemonium and the Primal Wild</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>You realize neatly cataloging splats like this goes explicitly against what the corebook says to do in these circumstances? Namely? that you shouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T16:23:32-08:00","id":1050136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1050038#post1050038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You realize neatly cataloging splats like this goes explicitly against what the corebook says to do in these circumstances? Namely? that you shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. There are a hundred variations starting from there. I can see an Invictus vampire radiating Arcadian energies, only to have it superseded by Primal symbols from his mastery of Protean.<br /> <br /> My Join Date may be relatively recent, but I've been lurking around these forums long enough, way before actually opening up an account, to know that the real fun of Mage comes from breaking down expectations and categories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T16:40:31-08:00","id":1050144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1049644#post1049644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spell actually says it identifies &quot;whether&quot; a subject is connected to the Supernal. In the case of a Sleeper you would get a negative response. Same would go for other supernatural creatures like werewolves and vampires, and if you tried to read deeper on those by using the Reach clause you get a jumble of confusing information that doesn't actually make any sense unless you've examined more of their kind to get some kind of context and even then it would just be, &quot;Oh, this thing looks like that other thing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Not sure I'd fully agree with this from my own read from it.<br /> <br /> ... That said, assuming one was using this read of that - would that also imply that a Sleepwalker who was only made a sleepwalker due to their own powers or powers gifted to them (such as by a vampire transforming a sleeper into a ghoul) would come up 'negative' to this read (thus sparking IC debates over what normal sleepwalker's connection was)... or would it imply that such a being has the capability to connect a normal person to the Supernal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T16:55:31-08:00","id":1050152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1050144#post1050144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Not sure I'd fully agree with this from my own read from it.<br /> <br /> ... That said, assuming one was using this read of that - would that also imply that a Sleepwalker who was only made a sleepwalker due to their own powers or powers gifted to them (such as by a vampire transforming a sleeper into a ghoul) would come up 'negative' to this read (thus sparking IC debates over what normal sleepwalker's connection was)... or would it imply that such a being has the capability to connect a normal person to the Supernal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule it as they show a connection to the Supernal but using the follow-up questions they have no Gnosis, and no connection to a particular Supernal Realm. That really ought to be enough to figure out what they are. Remember that the term Sleepwalker is something that Mages came up with to taxonimize a phenomena that they've observed in certain individuals because they just can't stop labeling shit they may or may not fully comprehend. It's not likely to be a category just divinely handed to them from the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:36:07-08:00","id":1050172,"title":"","content":"That is generally true of mages, but the fact is that Sleepwalker has a very solid definition based on something that I think Prime should have no problem discerning: They don't suffer Quiescence. The only two groups that have actual Supernal ties are mages and Proximi, and both are mentioned separately from Sleepwalkers in the spell's description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:32:07-08:00","id":1050250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1050172#post1050172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is generally true of mages, but the fact is that Sleepwalker has a very solid definition based on something that I think Prime should have no problem discerning: They don't suffer Quiescence. The only two groups that have actual Supernal ties are mages and Proximi, and both are mentioned separately from Sleepwalkers in the spell's description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this yeah. My thoughts are, if it wasn't designed to tell the difference and only to test: Supernal, yes/no , why waste the word space to put them there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T01:35:37-08:00","id":1050365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1050250#post1050250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically this yeah. My thoughts are, if it wasn't designed to tell the difference and only to test: Supernal, yes/no , why waste the word space to put them there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I already explained that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T04:47:42-08:00","id":1050428,"title":"","content":"I actually agree that it might be the intended interpretation, but I think it's worded quite badly, and is also a bad way using that spell. It just adds a step to get information that I think this spell should already be able to give you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T05:18:58-08:00","id":1050437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049468-supernal-vision-crossover?p=1050428#post1050428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually agree that it might be the intended interpretation, but I think it's worded quite badly, and is also a bad way using that spell. It just adds a step to get information that I think this spell should already be able to give you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the spell is worded in a way that leaves it open to more than one interpretation. That's just how I'd run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member",